# Folkprotocol Audit Triage v0
#
# Eighth experimental slice. It resolves conflicts among the citation, content,
# and tone audits without editing the draft or treating every stylistic
# suggestion as automatically compatible with factual fidelity.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Codex: """Triage the completed audits for
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md.

Required inputs are 00-commission.md, 70-practice-strains.md,
80-practice-assessment.md, 90-protocol-dossiers.md, 100-factual-draft.md,
110-tone-brief.md, 120-tone-draft.md, 130-citation-audit.md,
131-content-audit.md, and 132-tone-audit.md. Verify all completion markers.
Verify that each audit is current by recomputing its exact documented digest
from research/source-maps/{slug}/:

- 130: `sha256sum 00-commission.md 10-reddit-forums.md 20-traditional.md
  30-published-research.md 40-commercial-web.md 50-experimental-communities.md
  60-practitioner-folk-web.md 70-practice-strains.md
  80-practice-assessment.md 90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md
  120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`
- 131: `sha256sum 00-commission.md 70-practice-strains.md
  80-practice-assessment.md 90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md
  120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`
- 132: `sha256sum 110-tone-brief.md 120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`

If an audit is stale or incomplete, do not write the output; report the exact
file and stop.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the triage input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 70-practice-strains.md 80-practice-assessment.md
90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md 110-tone-brief.md
120-tone-draft.md 130-citation-audit.md 131-content-audit.md
132-tone-audit.md | sha256sum`. Write it as inputDigest in
research/source-maps/{slug}/133-audit-triage.md. If a completed triage records
the same digest, leave it unchanged.

Read only the required files and the existing output. The six source maps from
10 through 60 may be passed to sha256sum for the 130 currency check but must not
otherwise be read. Do no web research and do not edit any input. Write only
133-audit-triage.md. Work yourself: do not delegate, spawn subagents, or start
another agent workflow.

Account for every finding from all three audits. Mark each `accept`, `reject`,
or `already repaired`, with an exact phrase and a concise reason. A rejection
must cite the conflicting source, dossier, commission requirement, or factual
constraint; preference alone is not enough. Citation support and factual
fidelity take priority over a smoother sentence. A tone repair is invalid if it
would remove a useful effect size, exact community amount, source-access
boundary, population limit, or material qualification; strengthen a scoped
negative into a universal one; turn a failed search into proof of absence;
turn an observational association into causation; or introduce an unsupported
contrast. Necessary source-kind language is not report voice merely because it
names the kind of record.

If any accepted finding remains unresolved in 120-tone-draft.md, end with
`AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — REPAIR REQUIRED — N findings`. If every finding is
either already repaired or rejected with support, end with
`AUDIT TRIAGE COMPLETE — READY`. Do not write READY merely because an audit
itself used the word CLEAN.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, timeout=1200
